Package: elle
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.11),
         python3-pydantic,
         python3-httpx,
         python3-ruamel.yaml,
         python3-rich,
         python3-prompt-toolkit,
         python3-toml,
         libaugeas0,
         augeas-tools,
         polkitd,
         systemd
Recommends: ollama,
            python3-fastapi,
            python3-uvicorn,
            elled-telemetryd
Suggests: python3-bcc,
          libgirepository1.0-dev,
          gir1.2-atspi-2.0
Description: Enabling Layer Learning Everything
 A local-first, agentic system layer for Ubuntu that converts
 kernel-level telemetry into natural language insight and safe
 system operations.
 .
 ELLE provides:
  - Natural language interface for system administration
  - Man Vault: searchable man page index with semantic search
  - Incident Vault: decision memory for pattern matching
  - Intent classification before any system mutation
  - Polkit-gated privilege escalation
 .
 Requires Ollama for local LLM inference (recommended, not required
 for package installation).

Package: elled-ebpfd
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         libbpf1,
         libjansson4
Recommends: elle
Description: ELLE eBPF Telemetry Collector
 CO-RE (Compile Once - Run Everywhere) eBPF collector for ELLE.
 Provides high-performance kernel-level telemetry using libbpf.
 .
 Features:
  - OOM kill tracing
  - Process execution tracing
  - Block I/O latency tracking
  - TCP retransmission monitoring
  - Capability denial tracing
  - File permission denial tracing
  - Mount operation monitoring
 .
 This package is optional. If not installed, ELLE falls back to
 the BCC-Python eBPF implementation.

Package: elled-probed
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         libjansson4,
         libsystemd0
Recommends: elle
Description: ELLE Userspace Probe Collector (deprecated)
 Userspace polling collector for ELLE providing ground truth
 telemetry from system interfaces.
 .
 NOTE: This package is deprecated. Use elled-telemetryd instead,
 which provides all functionality in a unified daemon.
 .
 Features:
  - PSI pressure monitoring (memory, CPU, I/O stalls)
  - Systemd unit state tracking with crash loop detection
  - DNS health probing
  - Conntrack statistics and exhaustion detection
  - Hardware error monitoring (EDAC memory errors)
  - Authentication failure aggregation
 .
 This package complements elled-ebpfd by providing userspace
 telemetry that cannot be captured via eBPF.

Package: elled-telemetryd
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         libjansson4,
         libsystemd0,
         libpcre2-8-0,
         libssl3
Recommends: elle
Suggests: libbpf1
Conflicts: elled-ebpfd, elled-probed
Replaces: elled-ebpfd, elled-probed
Description: ELLE Unified Telemetry Daemon
 Unified telemetry collector for ELLE that combines eBPF tracing,
 journald monitoring, and userspace probes into a single daemon.
 .
 Features:
  - eBPF tracing (optional, requires libbpf):
    * OOM kill tracing
    * Process execution tracing
    * Block I/O latency tracking
    * TCP retransmission monitoring
    * Capability denial tracing
    * File permission denial tracing
    * Mount operation monitoring
  - Journald and kernel log streaming
  - Docker container event monitoring
  - File system change monitoring (inotify)
  - Periodic probes:
    * PSI pressure monitoring
    * Memory and swap usage
    * Disk space monitoring
    * Network interface errors
    * Thermal monitoring
    * Package change detection
    * Port listener detection
  - Event normalization with 58 category patterns
  - Deduplication with 60-second window
 .
 This package replaces elled-ebpfd and elled-probed, providing
 all functionality in a unified, lower-memory daemon (<20MB).
